WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.880
Vaati: This area and what happened here long ago

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.820
is what Maria hides behind the Astral Clocktower

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.420
This is the Fishing Hamlet

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.600
the third and final stage of Bloodborne's DLC

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.760
Beneath the surface, off to the left and the right,

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:20.980
is the city of Yharnam

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.020
The Nightmare we progressed through, from this perspective at least,

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.720
resided beneath the great lake all along

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.100
which explains why all the patients in the previous episode

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.660
heard the dripping, and the currents, and the rain

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.420
I went through the footage actually, because I was curious,

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.140
and, just before the clock tower opened,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.380
both hands aligned on one of the many runes that line the edges of the clock

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:51.880
Guess which one it was?
They pointed to a Deep Sea Rune. It reads:

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:57.760
"This transcription of the Great Ones' inhuman voices depicts downreaching currents.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:04.260
This rune means 'Deep Sea'. Great volumes of water serve as a bulwark guarding sleep,

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:10.500
and an augur of the eldritch Truth. Overcome this hindrance and seek what is yours"

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:18.580
The truths hidden here have to do with the Byrgenwerth scholars who violated this small fishing village long ago

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.680
Befuddled Villager: "Byrgenwerth... Byrgenwerth...

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.180
Blasphemous murderers... blood-crazed fiends...

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.820
Attonement for the wretches... By the wrath of Mother Kos...

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.440
Mercy for the poor, wizened child...

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.640
Mercy, oh please..."

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.320
Vaati: There's a lot in this dialogue

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:51.520
Firstly, this inhabitant of the village had some interaction with the scholars of Byrgenwerth,

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:58.340
the 'wretches' as he calls them. The murderers, the blood-crazed fiends, they did something to a child

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:04.400
and he calls upon the wrath of Mother Kos, who's name should probably be familiar to you, right?

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:09.740
Micolash: "Ahh, Kos, or some say Kosm...

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.040
Do you hear our prayers?"

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.360
Vaati: Clearly, she's a Great One.
As recommended by a couple of people in the last video

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:25.880
if you come here as a piece of cauliflower then instead the villager says this:

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:33.560
Befuddled Villager: "Curse here, curse there. A curse for he, and she, why care.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:42.940
A bottomless curse, a bottomless sea, source of all greatness, all things that be.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:52.180
Listen for the baneful chants. Weep with them, as one in trance.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:59.460
And weep with us, oh, weep with us..."

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:05.940
Vaati: So what did those of Byrgenwerth do to warrant curses being placed upon them?

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.060
It must have been pretty terrible and the accursed brew reads:

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:17.020
"Skull of a local from the violated fishing village. The inside of the skull was forcibly searched for eyes,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:24.100
as evidenced by the innumerable scratches and indentations. No wonder the skull became stewed in curses"

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:30.640
And this skull partly explains it. It sounds like the scholars of Byrgenwerth came to this little village

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.660
and violated the inhabitants in the name of new discoveries.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:40.240
And it also sounds like the villagers called upon a Great One to curse the scholars.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:45.100
According to the Moon Rune, the Great Ones are sympathetic in spirit, after all

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:50.140
and based on the way the Byrgenwerth scholars were violating them and searching them for eyes,

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.960
clearly the villagers had had some interaction with the Eldritch truth.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:04:01.040
So the scholars were cursed and so were their successors, the hunters.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:07.400
At this point, I went back and I unlocked all the cells we found in episode 1, do you remember those?

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.220
They were just past Ludwig.
According to this key,

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:16.840
hunters are held within the underground cells so that things better left unseen and better left unknown

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:23.760
will decay quietly. Within the first few cells, we find this church pick hunter. He drops the church pick

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:28.540
which is a sort of pickaxe crossed with a short sword or a spear type thing

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:33.220
And I also unlocked the door that held this guy who was reciting something

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:39.120
about being a true blade of the Church. According to the wikis, his only purpose is to be killed

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:45.520
and looted for his set which names him as Yamamura the Wanderer, an Eastern warrior

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:50.880
who pursued a beast for honorable revenge and then became a hunter of the league.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:56.180
The innermost cell belonging to the bell ringer remains locked. For now.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.740
Bell Ringer: "Do you hear this?

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.760
Fear the bell's toll.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.880
For only death awaits foolish prying eyes,

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:11.240
and the Church assassins are never far behind."

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.040
Vaati: Clearly there's more to discover so now that the stage is set,

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:19.180
let's play our part and get through to the finale

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:24.880
I love how this stage feels like an actual fishing village. They've done a great job with that.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:29.220
It's a unique location for a level as far as the Soulsborne series goes

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:34.560
and they do so much with such a simple theme. 
The fishmen are a dime a dozen

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.920
and I like how back stabs are actually a viable technique against them,

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:44.540
unlike most enemies in Bloodborne up until this point.
The fishmen attack in packs and they serve

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:49.600
as the standard enemy but the real threat are the giant fish troll things.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:54.800
The most scary enemy, in my opinion, is the one that can outrun your player character

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.200
and just look at how this thing moves when I turn my back on it.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.140
It scared the shit out of me right there

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:05.840
Approximately 1000 back stabs later, you learn just how difficult these things are

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:10.240
Maybe I should've used those obviously placed fire pots against it

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.720
Hmm. A note for next time

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:18.220
Hidden on the cliff face, also, is a path back to the ladder that was in front of the starting lantern

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:24.060
The player who pays attention is more likely to have checked for a hidden path back, which is a nice touch

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:28.660
And it is pretty worth it to look around all the time. 
Look at this thing

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:34.620
I noped out of here pretty quick. I didn't really fancy one of those things attacking me on a ladder

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:41.680
And I have to say, again, I really like the way this bit is designed. I only looked around because I started to hear

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:46.700
the Winter Lanterns singing and that's a kind of sound you want to watch out for

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:50.500
and it rewarded me by telling me there's a giant fish troll on the roof

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:56.020
You guys are probably realizing that I really like when games reward the observant player

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.520
I've probably said that a lot of times by now

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:03.980
So this next thing that happened probably happened to all of you guys too, right?

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:07.720
You start fighting one of the fish trolls and you know, you convince yourself

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:11.300
that other one on the roof isn't gonna come attack me. That's not gonna happen

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:16.300
And then you're about to win and you're like, hang on, what's that noise?

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:22.760
Godammit. One of these things was tough enough but two?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:27.940
I ran away and I got up the ladder just in time and I was gonna plan my next attack

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.380
And then I fell in.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:33.020
Don't worry, I survived until I got out and then I was like

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:37.920
'I know, I'll drop those rope Molotov cocktails behind me. They can fall down ladders, right?'

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:40.260
Uhh, no. Turns out they can't

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.620
And then I fell in again (Seriously Vaati?)

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:45.540
And at this point, I just made plunging attacks a part of my strategy

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:47.840
It didn't work, really...

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:54.800
Eventually I just 'got gud' and I realized, to my surprise, that one of them had dropped a weapon

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.720
It was the Rakuyo which is Maria's weapon

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:03.260
It reads: "Hunter weapon wielded by Lady Maria of the Astral Clocktower

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:10.740
A trick sword originating in the same country as the Cainhurst Chikage, only this sword feeds not off blood,

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:17.420
but instead demands great dexterity. Lady Maria was fond of this aspect of the Rakuyo,

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:22.660
as she frowned upon blood blades, being a distant relative of the queen.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:30.020
One day, she abandoned her beloved Rakuyo, casting it into a dark well, when she could stomach it no longer."

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.060
What a neat little story.

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:36.000
Maria must have eventually given into her desire for blood

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:40.740
as she certainly uses blood and self-sacrifice in her boss fight.

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:44.820
How curious that she's related to Queen Annalise, as well

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:48.940
I've got some theories on this but it'll have to wait for Prepare to Cry

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:53.200
By the end of the playthrough, the Rakuyo becomes my main weapon

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:57.600
This is a skill build after all, using the Blades of Mercy, the Burial Blade

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:02.140
and not to mention this character actually looks just like Maria, right?

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:08.300
I modeled this character after the Doll ages ago so yeah, who would've thought that would pay off?

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:12.500
It's cool to have a weapon that you can call your own, you know?

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:16.640
I've been searching for one for a while and mine is the Rakuyo.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:18.600
What's yours? You should let me know!

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:23.940
In a hut further down, we find a lantern and lying on the ground,

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:28.140
dying next to that lantern is Simon, the Bowblade Hunter

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:34.760
Simon: "...Oh, you, I'm afraid, I've made a botch of things...

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.160
...I can hear the bell, now...

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:44.720
...The beast-hide assassin, he's after me...

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.540
...Again and again...

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:56.760
...It never ends... (gasp)

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:02.260
...Please, I need you to do something...

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:09.140
...This village is the true secret. Testament to the old sins...

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.600
...It feeds this Hunter's Nightmare...

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:18.740
...Please, bring to an end the horror...

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:22.200
...So our forefathers sinned?

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.920
...We hunters cannot bear their weight forever...

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:34.020
...It isn't fair, it just isn't fair..."

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:39.280
(last breath)

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:46.620
Vaati: Simon was one of the last sane hunters in the Nightmare

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:51.340
He pushed us to go deeper and deeper into it and with Maria gone,

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:57.220
he seems like he decided to come forward himself and fight a little bit farther

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:01.500
However, there is another hunter here, other than Simon

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:06.200
Someone who doesn't want anyone discovering what lies at the end of the Nightmare

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.940
Brador, the Church Assassin

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:14.600
The weapon he uses is the Bloodletter "which assumes it's true and terrifying form

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:19.480
after it draws upon blood from the inner reaches of one's body and soul"

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:20.960
This is what it reads.

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.700
This was the only effective method of expelling tainted blood

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:29.480
or so Brador, isolated in his cell, continued to believe

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:33.540
Brador: "Well, well, look who's here.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:42.060
Welcome to my quarters. I've never entertained a guest before.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.360
Are you going to kill me?

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:53.560
After all you've done, kill me, as if to right your wrongs?

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.940
(laughter)

00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:02.380
You get his weapon if you kill him but I kept Brador alive here because I wasn't sure if there was more to him

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:07.380
and sure enough, he does invade you a total of 4 times throughout the rest of the stage.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:14.160
Once outside his cell, once on a bridge, once in ambush when you pick up an item down below

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.160
and once in a cave.

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:22.400
Each time he drops a different piece of his attire.
The clothing has it's own story as well.

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:28.880
Turns out, Brador was a Church assassin who wore the beast-hide of his former compatriots.

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:36.920
The Church gave him a bell that he could ring to hunt people down and stop people discovering their secrets

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:40.260
And we'll talk more about him later but moving on...

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:45.340
In the next section, I spied one of those mollusc things clinging to a post

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:49.040
and I was like 'yeah, I'm not gonna let myself get ambushed by that thing'

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:52.760
I still remembered how one of them fell on me in an earlier level

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:56.380
and then I was like worried about looking upwards and

00:12:56.380 --> 00:13:01.480
hundreds of them crawled out of shells and ambushed me and I felt pretty stupid

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:06.300
But seriously, do you remember that first one that fell out of the sky in episode 1?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:16.640
It makes sense now, doesn't it? All along there was this world above us, we just didn't have the insight to see it

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:21.680
And how this one fell out of the Nightmare itself is beyond me

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:26.380
But it's a cool concept to think that all of these Nightmares are layered.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:31.180
It makes me think about the ship masts all over the ocean as we progress

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:35.240
Think about it. You've actually seen these ship masts before

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.960
You can actually see them in the Nightmare Frontier,

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.740
suggesting that there's water down there, hidden in the fog

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:48.440
Or perhaps that the Nightmare Frontier is even connected to this Nightmare but is even higher up

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:53.500
After all, in the first stage of the DLC, there's an Amygdala corpse as well

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.660
Perhaps it fell out of the Nightmare frontier as well

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:01.800
This is really speculation but interesting to think about

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:08.100
To quote the Cosmic Eye Watcher Badge:
"Here we stand, feet planted in the earth,

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:13.220
but might the cosmos be very near us, only just above our heads?"

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:20.400
All of the Nightmare realms are really high up and they all have Great Ones residing at some of their highest points

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:26.660
Land masses float in the Nightmare frontier with Mergo in his loft in the tallest tower

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:32.380
The Hunter's Dream is nestled amongst these archtree looking things in the clouds

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:35.020
with the Moon Presence descending from above

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:41.260
And the Hunter's Nightmare is within a great ocean, below a grand lake of mud

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:48.960
and on the beach of said lake is the washed up corpse of a Great One that was discovered long ago

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:50.620
(sobbing)

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:56.340
Born from this corpse is the Orphan of Kos

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:01.920
How curious that the Orphan's mother wasn't alive for the birth

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:07.820
It reminds me of how the Moon Presence must die for us to be born as a Great One as well

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:17.000
This is probably one of the hardest bosses in Bloodborne

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:23.340
The Orphan is insanely quick, he has a hugely varied move set and he even has a second phase where he

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:26.780
evolves into a butterfly looking thing

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:34.560
The neat little observations in this fight are that he's fighting you with the placenta that trailed out with him

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:40.040
when he was born and also that Mother Kos herself has a face

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:43.800
Turns out she's somewhat humanoid in form just like he is

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:47.000
And I actually can't help myself,

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:52.020
I start talking about gameplay and then I get pulled back to talking about the lore again

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:58.080
I kind of figure that you guys are realizing how good the gameplay has been for the most part in this level

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:03.980
It's been an amazing stage but let's just roll with it, let's just talk about the story

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:07.520
while I show you some of my failed fights against this guy

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:13.480
Specifically, let's talk about why our character is here, why we're doing all of this

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:17.260
We do have most of the items and dialogue now, after all

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:23.460
In the dialogue at the start, we learned that the Byrgenwerth scholars stumbled upon this fishing village

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:26.380
and that they did some pretty terrible things

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:32.380
Not only did they violate the villagers themselves, as mentioned in the accursed brew description

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:39.720
But they must have also stumbled upon the Great One Kos or her corpse at least which washed up on the shore

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:42.580
because they managed to get themselves cursed

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:48.740
The man at the start of the village and even the woman speaking as you get pulled into the DLC, remember her?

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:56.520
Both of them plead for curses to be placed upon the fiends, upon their children and their children's children,

00:17:56.520 --> 00:18:01.920
on man and woman alike.
A bottomless curse, a curse forever true

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:09.160
And the Great Ones do have the power to curse people. According to the Defiled Chalice,

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:14.660
which is an item a lot of us probably have forgotten about, curses are, and I quote:

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:20.460
"caused by inciting the anger of the Great Ones"
Additionally, according to the Moon Rune:

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:23.740
as I've mentioned, the Great Ones are sympathetic in spirit

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:29.660
So it's not crazy to think that a Great One may have listened to the inhabitants of the fishing village

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:35.400
as they pleaded for the Byrgenwerth scholars to be cursed in return for violating their village

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:41.360
The curse means that the Byrgenwerth scholars and, eventually, their successors the hunters

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:47.580
would be drawn into a Hunter's Nightmare upon death.
And it's a pretty perfect curse when you think about it

00:18:47.840 --> 00:18:51.320
It's like the Great One is saying 'oh, you like hunting so much?

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:59.260
Well live here forever and hunt for all eternity then'.
Simon tells us that the village is the source of the sin

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:07.120
and implies that we can bring an end to the curse here. So we do what a hunter does best. We hunt.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:13.760
Voice: "...Ahh, sweet child of Kos, returned to the ocean...

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:24.860
A bottomless curse, a bottomless sea. Accepting of all that there is and can be."

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:33.320
Vaati: When you get back to the Hunter's Dream, the Doll will tell you that both she and Gerhman

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:37.100
sense that they've somehow been freed from their shackles

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:42.920
This happens to the Doll and Gerhman when you kill Maria and the Orphan respectively.

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:47.060
I'm starting to understand how they're connected to these creatures but

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:52.040
it is still really weird that they can sense their counterparts in the Nightmare

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:57.640
I'm still trying to figure it out. Hell, I personally haven't even got this dialogue yet because the Doll

00:20:57.640 --> 00:21:01.400
doesn't give you the dialogue if the dream is on fire, which is annoying

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.160
I'll have to play through again so I can show it to you

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:09.500
But... so much to talk about here. There's a million other things I want to talk to you guys about

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:13.360
There's even another boss in this DLC that I don't have time to include

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:17.180
But mostly I really wanna talk to you guys about the lore, still

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:24.120
This DLC revealed a ton about the timeline, it reveals a lot about how Nightmare realms work

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:27.700
and it's raised even more questions that I myself haven't answered

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:33.040
It's expanded the stories of Gerhman, of Micolash, of Laurence and the Doll

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:36.100
and all of those videos will be coming soon, I promise

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:40.760
